<Layout title="New to Orthodoxy?"><PageIntro title="An ancient faith. A living invitation." label="Explore Orthodoxy" description="Christianity is more than a set of ideas. It is a life in Christ, shared in worship, prayer, and community."/><div class="wrap page-body content-grid"><article class="prose"><h2>Begin with “come and see.”</h2><p>The Orthodox Church preserves the Christian faith handed down by Jesus Christ to His Apostles. Its worship and spiritual life invite us to become more like Christ, one day at a time.</p><p>At St. Peter, you are welcome to bring your questions. You do not need to understand everything before visiting. The best place to begin is with the people and prayer of the Church.</p><h2>Worship with the whole person.</h2><p>In Orthodox worship, we pray with words and silence, with hymns and Scripture, with icons and incense. The Divine Liturgy is at the heart of our life together.</p><p>Visitors are welcome to observe and take part in the prayers. Father Hans can help you understand what you experience and guide your next steps.</p><h2>A faith to live every day.</h2><p>Prayer, the Holy Sacraments, the Scriptures, and acts of love shape the Christian life. We learn to live this life together, supported by the Church.</p><p><a href="/sacraments/">Explore the Holy Sacraments</a>, read <a href="/the-creed/">the Nicene Creed</a>, or begin with <a href="/the-lords-prayer/">the Lord’s Prayer</a>.</p><div class="notice">Interested in learning more? Contact the parish about opportunities for instruction and conversation with Father Hans.</div><a class="button" href="/visit/">Visit us this Sunday <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></article><Sidebar/></div></Layout>
